[{"id":"VRCE-2-27-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":1,"english":"Being consoled thus by Rāma, Maithilī, the daughter of Janaka, fearing separation, lovingly and haughtily laughed at Rāghava of spacious breast, and spoke to him, her husband, the following words with a view to follow him to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf0b809eadbf56f9a91446c6be30c618b2c8b2e758f241ec025dce6b68bb4f4c","compact":"745d30cb6c03162d3faf7ff24cc2bf11e9b20a5dc56efe2acbcd4fdc73116ef7","nasal":"65446efeedfcc773415342004e12eefa3cb1f785c18a862e4cc672a8e38d19d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":2,"english":"Being consoled thus by Rāma, Maithilī, the daughter of Janaka, fearing separation, lovingly and haughtily laughed at Rāghava of spacious breast, and spoke to him, her husband, the following words with a view to follow him to the forest.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"102e8e3d696e0a06c3ab947a34468b507f95c01fc7c3edada3d3dfb5ef77d10c","compact":"388be73c2ad7f2fd32e0e8a347009067b16f355af560722a5da144101511dd44","nasal":"6f798cd25eef09bf493065c1f7dc89318bae84bd4fd28f3540e0457955fcbe86"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":3,"english":"What thought of you, O Rāma, my father, the king of Mithilā, accepting you as his son-in-law, who was a man if form but (in deeds)a woman?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"994794c2cbe04917b55ca7f8b0d698fae6d28cf1148f10b4eafea80d6da6d9f4","compact":"b1a242d6005b08d7255f4e8363fecab8908751f9d62cf1a1701fa389512bea53","nasal":"b1a242d6005b08d7255f4e8363fecab8908751f9d62cf1a1701fa389512bea53"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":4,"english":"Henceforth, if people through ignorance say that the sun has not that burning flood of light which in Rāma does shine forth, woe is them, it is falsehood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6393bc4002b01a5f0b7096ed58cf665f2a71a529ddd15f09700db9c688ca5915","compact":"b45f7d961c59cf0436fef4f424be50ffefefc243f2bdc65ec33b254eb3a8bc8b","nasal":"b45f7d961c59cf0436fef4f424be50ffefefc243f2bdc65ec33b254eb3a8bc8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":5,"english":"Why are you so dejected and whence is your fear that you are willing to leave behind your wife who has none else but you?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cecabe7522de21f00bb13ec1bacbeec743dcab06b3f23eb2a8dc45fa37f7e7dc","compact":"24e21796f5f259cea635595e7e0f0c5a18fce29bbf18ae9f8eda87909223ece4","nasal":"e805bf59713aa681b0bd425837443feb8e2870cb4159a22bced1f459c8cee88e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":6,"english":"Know me to be perfectly under your influence like to Sāvitri, following her husband Satyavān, the son of Dyumatsen.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.851,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fea954aeb17f3393799448fff77a463d5fffcb0bc5effec2d42c49890a8f58c1","compact":"0791e4c715fa122ec0de342b0a97bbf8dba8bce67f738b7ac45581eeaf17654b","nasal":"5fd546aaf7d3a746542ad0269923d0ac03a3ba39cdb3d28d1ee5ac098cca6d2e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":7,"english":"I have not, like one bringing stigma on her line, ever in my life thought of a second person, but of you whom I must follow into the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"61cfbea23ef1c43205fab2e73ca59517353cfe4b1302aafb7d48de78b956b24d","compact":"7b55539b686fbdbab1095796a66b9f9ae920f8c1a8d1b67b4da11972b80b4f95","nasal":"7b55539b686fbdbab1095796a66b9f9ae920f8c1a8d1b67b4da11972b80b4f95"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":8,"english":"Do you, like to an ordinary actor, wish to hand me over to others, who am chaste, pure as a virgin, and long held in conjugal affection?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"18aca981318b66affcec83ce250f3312902630c31610bb3411adde77d5b1ea69","compact":"aa024a8645713e3f14f0a95b307b85a9891326a43b41014e42e1d3db52021073","nasal":"aa024a8645713e3f14f0a95b307b85a9891326a43b41014e42e1d3db52021073"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":9,"english":"It does not behove you to repair to the forest without taking me along with you. Be it the austerity of an ascetic, the forest or heaven, with you will I be everywhere.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e7965bfe1a417d4c17d993ca83e53bfa9e9ba38e638efe4fb94aaeee6740c80","compact":"fd0781fd3027a174bd09678717ed26e48a1d2f08c7aa373968ddb6c06efbf987","nasal":"fd0781fd3027a174bd09678717ed26e48a1d2f08c7aa373968ddb6c06efbf987"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":10,"english":"No toil shall I suffer on the way, as if lying on a bed of luxury, while following you in they footstep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.966,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a119140447ab886676c8b286bf582b52c18cca5ed87eed1c21891a7c8f298d0","compact":"1c8ecdfcc5682f91a9ebfdeb2a08dec2cae32c4dea0f0290d242745d562c6f74","nasal":"b2218576ca08b806424702820b60d74076afa221f2e9665feffcaa6b01294153"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":11,"english":"When with you, the various thorny grasses, the Kuśa, the Käsa, the Sara, and the Işika, and the thistles and brambles on the way, shall be to me in touch like to linen and deer-skin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ea5ced1b9cfae05893d012051eb9838487bdb753c14cdd1622dc7e792a1fba6","compact":"53de7ca114167bf0e1c85e969056dfb15409d2a135cad59f30111c0d663dccc3","nasal":"8362dda0617d46513ec84ace2a16fd53937947a628bdcac8f9e828d44c443eca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":12,"english":"The dust that will cover me, thrown up by the gush of wind shall be, O ravisher of my heart regarded by me as the finest sandal dust.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f9f496f500ec8ded5ab7914d1200a628e833d32824413d46bf2ebd2c7f362ce","compact":"f0fe9e9d44021d11c4806fd975bcd578093ee8adc385a4165ca361b807118ad0","nasal":"3c435f9b1252ece7a571e3e751938db8833b24d4e995a4aa507349c4879b645a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":13,"english":"When I shall lie down on the bed of green grass in the forest, it shall appear to me more pleasant than one covered with a coloured blanket.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"977dd875a018b3b970084493b9606d345b2330cb8d95e88072dd6272010310fb","compact":"bed91b2f4c0283ca36f49d9a84660436a77481f4efd07c93c4f34803e45f7dd3","nasal":"ce5277ee1ca74b7ea2ca9792e12871ee8fc9b5a011d9fcc09cb98d0ad0165da6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":14,"english":"Fruits, roots and leaves which you will bring yourself and give me, be they great or small in quantity, shall be to me like to the ambrosiajuice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.695,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d771f540daccfe0764b4f9a3a7abd2e3f835e32f5494554edeb2e60560c50038","compact":"a8586949181f4fb248f65b586d47c7888888fd82f22635b28b8b9363e56d4a0a","nasal":"a8586949181f4fb248f65b586d47c7888888fd82f22635b28b8b9363e56d4a0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":15,"english":"I shall never think of my father, mother, or my abode; I shall enjoy fruits and flowers growing in various seasons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a6907d9ba512c1299ab1cc364b8addc0a5d34673512ad1a07e12ef26f64f009","compact":"17d0d4daceeb90a9e147ca9919d63de368227f14b52ed15013d0ca8d5f370e7b","nasal":"9042df78ea5bbcbdc4c27f593a3da6b142694615415d037b0b336b707874be81"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":16,"english":"You shall not witness any thing disagreeable there; for me you shall not experience any sorrow, no shall I be a burden to you; do you take me with you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"467412e865c2fa64ccf54a411d6254641b2caa2e38763653c4dfa666b8350a20","compact":"49a5cdfd4158be8a241861f6fb851664627c41e3de57b97dba026c9c4b84cacb","nasal":"df9f71de6c55000fd136904c1e04f029c46858ba93a822932cc9eae06a593497"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":17,"english":"O, Rāma, conceiving with pleasure that your company is a heaven to me and your absence a hell. If you do not take me to the forest which I count freed from all evils, surely I shall drink poison and never come under the influence of my enemies.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d5b85a1edb71cb1558029be28944d36b6d1faac74763fbd44fd217935f18827","compact":"42d0986de74714e9775538152f995e62499954500c815f66d754b906a2a9800b","nasal":"42d0986de74714e9775538152f995e62499954500c815f66d754b906a2a9800b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":18,"english":"O, Rāma, conceiving with pleasure that your company is a heaven to me and your absence a hell. If you do not take me to the forest which I count freed from all evils, surely I shall drink poison and never come under the influence of my enemies.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.655,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a30a97bdd3e98ff7f2a75ca360ce72a497d10868554ec1d3b0f7eb839f35a9a8","compact":"450b2d5125898d65cea238b43fdcee2b55f8adcf8bfe4c8cfc1607d94369fc78","nasal":"450b2d5125898d65cea238b43fdcee2b55f8adcf8bfe4c8cfc1607d94369fc78"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":19,"english":"When through affliction I shall not live after separation, better it is, O Lord, that I die immediately at the time of my being forsaken by you; I cannot bear this grief even for a moment. How shall I be able to live without you for fourteen years?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aceef330f5c179b0dc7bf29798f4066059e87695d112805116fdca66e65a77bc","compact":"7c6ddcdfdf30a3bc581dda9cabe82d2cc9b624963cdd12097281673c5cbb0c56","nasal":"7c6ddcdfdf30a3bc581dda9cabe82d2cc9b624963cdd12097281673c5cbb0c56"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":20,"english":"When through affliction I shall not live after separation, better it is, O Lord, that I die immediately at the time of my being forsaken by you; I cannot bear this grief even for a moment. How shall I be able to live without you for fourteen years?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d59611cb4f0beec8fdea2edc2c1f79a51fe4fefdeec62c8651d33fe0dd48c077","compact":"204538c2aa1e6f90e21e41ffa5f6c84058863f4210abaac2502ceec317c208cb","nasal":"204538c2aa1e6f90e21e41ffa5f6c84058863f4210abaac2502ceec317c208cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":21,"english":"Thus lamenting, Sītā, racked with sorrow, embraced her husband and began to cry aloud.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d23f0566aebdaa9ce9698ed527c4448010d80b047b84cae39c87b4dcada23220","compact":"6d1e19591a77b0a3fc29a18cc428f33852e2592837f9d5a292bbb3cba8e76fd3","nasal":"7a83ae7a5c4a39e058d12491222eaadc94ced713e30ee257a8c63f70ac828b62"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":22,"english":"Like to a she-elephant, she being pierced by the poisonous shafts of Rāma's words, began to shed tears, long kept off, as an Araņi wood emits fire continually.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"96eca4dd9adb56354cfc1b3c8ff47b08280aff843114880f1d55c3b857268761","compact":"7f64a7d16ecea313459fdf762f8bdbb5846ad48c5f41da91ad705e7b3b7d8591","nasal":"a456fead9698299c525e5dcfeda8a0f57dd2803da15347ebad304f4ab3a22ccc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":23,"english":"Tears caused by her sorrow and white as the crystal began to trickle down from her eyes, like to water falling in drops from lotus petals.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8106d462dc197f4d573c15b922fcc3de59371e556f54d7cbd8028afe1cbf046","compact":"a0d1b0c679f0adbe5683e0067c32b63631f60ee1a338c471295ccb8f37f92313","nasal":"bf8f8493f942a21fa7a5eec0a55d55de2ccd71bfa44401ef30959a3431d2228a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":24,"english":"Finding her almost insensible with sorrow, Rāma flung his arms round her and reviving her (with consolation) spoke the following words to her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa1f808cd430855917aca57abfb0c0798dd4b2dc7fac2bf490fc40d9b478eb5b","compact":"4db51c8db717056a2a1c656b4713a43273e647ae2d5b45d4817fad94e37cf37f","nasal":"4db51c8db717056a2a1c656b4713a43273e647ae2d5b45d4817fad94e37cf37f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":25,"english":"I do not long for, Oh worshipful one, even the abode of celestials gained through your affliction; fear there is none for me like to the self-create Brahma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a6480e2f39816953aa59baa1c4080bc8b757d2516081d45a09e469d3bae50fd","compact":"2de2d5e9c9ea09e0665d737fc860b97c7ca02c7a9e78ace2c7d32957e23f6591","nasal":"009b6cc6d25a85a8de39fd4c081c13dc75d500f3adf2365124333376ecfd507e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":26,"english":"Not apprised of your full intention, O you of beautiful countenance, I could not, though capable of escorting you, desire your abode in the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027026","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cbfd32d49831c233cff6e087b6758b383e466d3c0f4f5029df39f54b11635a1","compact":"525aa4a671ab7d32a33e11abe42b764aaa1ab154732ecb287bc73575f0d800bb","nasal":"525aa4a671ab7d32a33e11abe42b764aaa1ab154732ecb287bc73575f0d800bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-27","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":27,"english":"When you are determined O Maithili, repair to the forest with me, I cannot leave you behind, as one possessing self-knowledge cannot renounce munificence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027027","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"334bd62b10b329e63d046a5ad9e6b9c21d0a0dfcb81f5f6e1553ebee0172cb9f","compact":"b4ec2d87faa04badbf7da1b5b569cdabc33b79990f5035889adcf00c538388e3","nasal":"b4ec2d87faa04badbf7da1b5b569cdabc33b79990f5035889adcf00c538388e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-28","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":28,"english":"O you, having thighs resembling the trunks of an elephant, I shall resort to that virtue which was exercised by great and good men going before, do you follow me therefore like Suvarcalā following the Sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4154707ce570faff288fd12fb8a9543249a9a2c479a0236ef47737e44b68cb4","compact":"670ae5f98d517271276ad20e915d2034c89922226ac74c98247fc59a5f8d8c32","nasal":"670ae5f98d517271276ad20e915d2034c89922226ac74c98247fc59a5f8d8c32"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":29,"english":"Obedience to his parents is the virtue of a son. Disobeying the command of my father I am not eager to live. we","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7e1e74164bc984b21d5268e55e36e10fbdd5916c9021646eb0d3b147ff992eb","compact":"13b4eb2a8b7f885e964d613d55cc69055742d23362ba372f64828076a5396a03","nasal":"13b4eb2a8b7f885e964d613d55cc69055742d23362ba372f64828076a5396a03"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":30,"english":"Therefore do I desire to follow what my father commands me, treading in the path of truth, and this is the virtue eternal.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.632,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a6148aa0b5510167dd525c3dff53af0411daa6c1eb25292abb57ae42ea593ae4","compact":"62c9d76b56adca12756c8eafc181a1518022ea9c3d697b0b0b9207f56961fb24","nasal":"62c9d76b56adca12756c8eafc181a1518022ea9c3d697b0b0b9207f56961fb24"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":31,"english":"Do you give away jewels to the Brāhmaṇas and edibles to the beggars longing for them, and make haste without delay.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36c42598f014efc05cc36f7745bd485f07c0dfd06de4fbf8334b0627195c2b85","compact":"63ea00b5fa692e87a75fb3a9a626721a2644b33e253a56ad5a67ade971ab34a0","nasal":"63ea00b5fa692e87a75fb3a9a626721a2644b33e253a56ad5a67ade971ab34a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":32,"english":"Confer upon the Brāhmaṇas, valuable ornaments, excellent clothes, pleasant toys, beds, conveyances and other fine things in your possession and then what remains do you distribute amongst the servants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4323b7597462ee4dfc1b66895f62b3dcf9e512397c311eaf83ad1a5b0a5ded13","compact":"19ef817657cd933e55ce4a129c8553112feea35c95c1ae8d4f69dfd838a4e15d","nasal":"19ef817657cd933e55ce4a129c8553112feea35c95c1ae8d4f69dfd838a4e15d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-27-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":27,"verse":33,"english":"Convinced that her going to the forest was desired by her husband, Sītā began to distribute them speedily with a delighted heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.916,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-30-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2027033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd635c1893610d4d6c731ffea3c480ba273ef3ba80b092165c28b2db99d55087","compac